I've only ascended once, so my end-game experience is somewhat limited,
but here's what I would get rid of:

- 55 shuriken: I know I'll get flamed for this, but... ditch 'em. With
700 HP and -52 AC, dual-wielding GS and silver saber, you can mow down
pretty much anything in meelee. Avoid, wand-zap or genocide whatever
you really don't want to get close to (mindflayers, *trices, grabbing
monsters, etc.). At least keep those shuriken in the BoH most of the
time.
I'm not a fan of missile weapons, so I may be somewhat biased against
them. Your mileage may vary, I just don't think you'll ever need the
shuriken with those HP/AC stats.

- the small shield: when your AC is around -50, those 6 points from the
shield won't make a difference, believe me. Get rid of that thing, now.

- 10 wands of teleport: 5 are more than enough, I'd say.
- 10 wands of digging: dito, 5 should be enough if you take the direct
route to the portal on the plane of earth. Then drop them once you're
in the plane of air, you won't need them anymore after that (keep one
if you're concerned about being engulfed).
- 5 wands of fire/cold: I'd take 2 of each at most. You've got wands of
death and scrolls of charging.
- wand of probing: useless, especially when you have a stethoscope.
- wand of polymorph (0:0): while /oPoly won't be terribly useful in the
planes, an empty /oPoly isn't useful at all ;)

- 15 K-rations: 5-10 should be enough for any Famine-related accidents.
- 6 lizard corpses: 2 of 'em and you're set. Just be careful around
*trices and remember, you still have a set of =oLS if you really manage
to mess up... somehow.

- 6 potions of booze: just zap a spell you didn't refresh after 20k
turns, that will confuse you just fine.

- 26 scrolls of teleport: hmm, just dig out straight paths and walk
from stairwell to stairwell. Your idea is nice, but overkill in some
way ;)

- 10 scrolls of create monster: uh, what the hell? There's gonna be
enough summoned stuff on the astral plane for lots of conflict fun, you
definitely won't need those unless you want to build an acid blob fort.

- stethoscope: only keep it if you can cast healing spells reliably. No
need to monitor your dragon's HP if you can't do anything once they get
low.


Apart from that, I can't think of a way to further reduce weight.
You're probably even bringing additional stuff not listed here, such as
a unihorn, various tools (markers, light source, ...) and souvenirs.

Honestly, I'm somewhat surprised your BoH can't hold the stuff you
listed without making you burdened. I remember taking boatloads of
souvenirs and other assorted crap with me on my first ascension, and I
wasn't burdened. Are you sure the bag is blessed?



